  "rule": "R-17 - the slice declares its pair diffs here; the capture is its own commit"
 },
 "what_landed": [
  "damage.py grows one declared key on the empowers_next_auto vocabulary, rides_scheduled_auto: the empowerment is delivered by the fight's next scheduled swing at or after the cast instead of at the cast. _resolve_scheduled_auto_rides claims those swings once, after the keystone schedules are installed, and both the row's authored events and its target_debuff window read the claim.",
  "champions/jayce.py declares it on BOTH Transform branches. The cache gives Transform no attack-timer reset, so Cannon's armour/MR shred and Hammer's bonus magic both land on the swing they empower. Cannon R therefore carries a basic attack it never carried before, and MODULE_CC['R'] becomes a plain 'none' instead of per_part.",
  "champions/vex.py splits Shadow Surge into the Shadow's cached Magic Damage and the recast consume's, which the cached Total Magic Damage row sums exactly at every rank. MODULE_CC['R'] = 'none' follows, and Vex's last coarse source is gone."
 ],
 "qualifying_population": {
  "enumerated_before_first_src_edit": true,
  "rule": "Only two champion modules changed, so the qualifying set is the Jayce and Vex entries of champion_baselines plus every registered_champion_fights scenario whose attacker is Jayce or Vex. Nothing else in the snapshot reads the new timing: every other empowering entry leaves rides_scheduled_auto absent and keeps being timed at its cast.",
  "method": "'golden_snapshot.py compare scripts/golden_baseline.json --report' at the slice tip.",
  "measured": {
   "differing_leaves": 74,
   "qualifying_leaves": 73,
   "numeric_leaves": 46183,
   "leaf_ratio": 0.001602321200441721,
   "ratio_clause_triggered": false
  }
 },
 "why_each_family_moved": {
  "champion_baselines/Jayce/R": "the entry gains empowers_next_auto and a reviewed cc_kind, and its detail says 'no bonus damage' rather than 'no direct damage' - the row now carries the attack.",
  "champion_baselines/Vex/R": "one 375.0 part becomes 125.0 at t=0 and 250.0 at t=0.5 (level 11, 0 AP). The sum is the cached Total Magic Damage row, unchanged.",
  "registered_champion_fights/Jayce/<level>/<build> (burst, no autos)": "R's row goes from 0.0 to the basic attack the cast forces, and the fight total rises by exactly that. A spellblade build rises by one more proc as well: R is a cast, it arms a charge, and the swing it forces now exists to spend it.",
  "registered_champion_fights/Jayce/<level>/sustained/<build>": "two effects at once. One swing moves off auto_attacks onto R's row (attribution only), and the shred's 5-second window now opens at that swing instead of at t=0, so it covers less of the fight - every armour-mitigated row drops by the same 2.57 percent at level 18 (Q 514.04 -> 500.82, W 1175.30 -> 1145.08, autos before the move 1780.75 -> 1734.97).",
  "registered_champion_fights/Vex/*": "nothing moved. The recast's 0.5s offset sits well inside every scenario's window, so the two hits land where the one lump did and the totals are identical."
 },
